403
00:21:14,470 --> 00:21:17,850
[Peggy Talks Love Psychology]

404
00:21:16,330 --> 00:21:16,790
Hello, everyone.

405
00:21:16,790 --> 00:21:18,040
I'm Ms. Peggy.

406
00:21:18,040 --> 00:21:18,570
Today,

407
00:21:18,600 --> 00:21:19,870
I'm going to talk about

408
00:21:19,900 --> 00:21:21,540
the mere exposure effect.

409
00:21:21,540 --> 00:21:23,790
Mere exposure effect,

410
00:21:23,790 --> 00:21:26,040
also known as the familiarity principle,

411
00:21:26,040 --> 00:21:27,200
means that

412
00:21:27,200 --> 00:21:29,000
when something constantly appears

413
00:21:29,000 --> 00:21:30,160
in front of you,

414
00:21:30,160 --> 00:21:32,830
you will develop a preference for it.

415
00:21:32,830 --> 00:21:33,880
For example...

416
00:21:34,750 --> 00:21:37,550
Be honest with me.
You all love drinking, don't you?

417
00:21:37,550 --> 00:21:39,630
When you choose wine,

418
00:21:39,660 --> 00:21:40,790
you usually go for

419
00:21:40,820 --> 00:21:42,410
brands you are familiar with, right?

420
00:21:41,760 --> 00:21:42,380
[What's Familiar Feels Right]

421
00:21:42,410 --> 00:21:44,660
Perhaps the ones that advertise a lot.

422
00:21:44,660 --> 00:21:45,810
And you might ignore

423
00:21:45,830 --> 00:21:47,580
those unfamiliar brands.

424
00:21:47,580 --> 00:21:49,830
This also applies to our relationships.

425
00:21:49,830 --> 00:21:51,410
For example, I've received
a lot of questions like this:

426
00:21:51,410 --> 00:21:53,130
"Ms. Peggy, I've had a crush on someone
for a long time,

427
00:21:53,130 --> 00:21:54,290
